<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A8.SS1.SSS1" title="In H.1 Proof of Theorem for Linear-Reasoning problem ‣ Appendix H Proofs of the Theorems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">H.1.1 </span>Define each <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as a proposition described in the given premises.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A8.SS1.SSS2" title="In H.1 Proof of Theorem for Linear-Reasoning problem ‣ Appendix H Proofs of the Theorems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">H.1.2 </span>The conditional probability <math class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P[X_{i}|Context,X_{1},\ldots,X_{i-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P[X_{i}|Context,X_{1},\ldots,X_{i-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as selecting the next proposition based on the augmented context.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A8.SS1.SSS3" title="In H.1 Proof of Theorem for Linear-Reasoning problem ‣ Appendix H Proofs of the Theorems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">H.1.3 </span>Fixed the LLM as a function <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}(Augmented\ Context)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}(Augmented\ Context)</annotation></semantics></math> as the correctness percentage of selecting the correct proposition from context. The values for different augmented contexts are assumed to be the same, defined as <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></a></li>
